---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const effective = 'November 8, 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy · Budget Pipeline"
  description="Privacy policy for Budget Pipeline, a personal read-only data pipeline by Michelle Lee."
  current="privacy"
>
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <a href="/budget-pipeline/">Budget Pipeline</a>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Effective {effective}</p>
  </div>

  <section class="wrap longform">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Budget Pipeline is a personal data pipeline built and used only by its author, Michelle Lee,
        on her own accounts. It is not offered to other users. This policy describes what data it
        accesses and how that data is handled.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Data accessed</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Gmail:</strong> with the read-only scope <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly</code>, the app reads order, shipping and refund emails sent from six amazon.com sender addresses in the author’s own mailbox. It does not read any other email.</li>
        <li><strong>Bank and card data:</strong> account balances and transactions from the author’s own accounts, through SimpleFIN with read-only access.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How data is used</h2>
      <p>
        Data is used only to build the author’s personal spending and net worth reports, for example
        matching Amazon order items to card charges. The app never sends, modifies or deletes email,
        and never moves money.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Storage and security</h2>
      <p>
        Data is stored only on the author’s own computer or in the author’s own database account.
        The Google OAuth token and other credentials are stored locally, are excluded from source
        control, and are never published.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        No data is shared with, sold to, or transferred to any third party. No data is used for
        advertising or to train AI or machine learning models.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Google API Services User Data Policy</h2>
      <p>
        Budget Pipeline’s use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Data is kept only as long as the author uses it for personal reporting, and can be deleted at
        any time by deleting the local database. Google access can be revoked at any time at
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>,
        after which the app can no longer read any email.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with a new effective date.</p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p>Michelle Lee · <a href="mailto:hello@michulee.com">hello@michulee.com</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
